   "id": "step-10",
   "title": "The cartridge: feed servo, dial, flywheel motors and the cartridge board",
   "text": "On the bench, not on the turret. The feed servo (its bus ID set to 3 beforehand) up against the dial floor's underside, its horn through the floor and its length to the rear: 4 x M2 x 6 flat heads from above, flush. The dial onto the horn: 4 x M3 x 8 down through the holes in its cone (the hopper off); set the servo's zero so a pocket is centred over the exit hole and write the count down. Each X2216 with its hub: the prop adapter from its box on the bell (3 x M2), the hub's flat face on the adapter's flange, its bore reamed to 5.00 on the pilot, the washer and an M5 nylon-insert nut (snug plus a quarter turn); turn it by hand with a dial indicator on the rim: under 0.15 mm, or re-seat; then the Ø34 tyre stretched on. Each motor goes up through the opening under its shell to the plate, its leads out through the slot: 4 x M3 x 6 in the radial slots (never longer: the motor has 2.8 mm of thread). The two AM32 ESCs on the cage plate on foam tape, each motor's leads to its ESC; the cartridge board on its four posts over them (4 x M3 x 6), the brake FETs' drains to the phase leads, and the pigtail to the two CT plugs (Gyropup's docs/turret-wiring.md).",
